## Associations

| Association | Type | Direction | Owner side (FK) | Result in database |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Agence` → `Employe` | OneToMany / ManyToOne | Bidirectional | `Employe.agence` | `employe.agence_id_agence` |
| `Agence` → `Vehicule` | OneToMany / ManyToOne | Bidirectional | `Vehicule.agence` | `vehicule.agence_id_agence` |
| `Maintenance` → `Vehicule` | ManyToOne | Unidirectional | `Maintenance.vehicule` | `maintenance.vehicule_id_vehicule` |
| `Vehicule` ↔ `Equipement` | ManyToMany | Bidirectional | `Vehicule.equipements` | join table `vehicule_equipements` |
| `Vehicule` → `Reservation` | OneToMany / ManyToOne | Bidirectional | `Reservation.vehicule` | `reservation.vehicule_id_vehicule` |
| `Client` → `Reservation` | OneToMany / ManyToOne | Bidirectional | `Reservation.client` | `reservation.client_id_client` |
| `Reservation` ↔ `Contrat` | OneToOne | Bidirectional | `Contrat.reservation` | `contrat.reservation_id_reservation` (unique) |
| `Contrat` → `Paiement` | OneToMany / ManyToOne (composition) | Bidirectional | `Paiement.contrat` | `paiement.contrat_id_contrat` (not null) |

### Mapping rules used

- The **owner side** holds the foreign key and has no `mappedBy`.
- The **inverse side** declares `mappedBy = "<field name in the owner entity>"`.
- Collections are `Set<...>` initialized with `new HashSet<>()`.
- `cascade = CascadeType.ALL` and `orphanRemoval = true` are used only for the **composition** `Contrat` → `Paiement`. A payment cannot exist without its contract.
- Entities use `@Getter` / `@Setter` instead of `@Data` to avoid infinite loops in `toString()`, `equals()` and `hashCode()` on bidirectional relations.
- Enumerations are stored as text with `@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)`.

